<rml>
<head>
	<title>typography</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<style>
		/*
			The metrics reference: the document --metrics-report is run against before and after
			anything that touches the text engine, comparing the two reports at the same size and
			dp ratio. Advances here are unhinted and scaled from design units, which is what lets
			one atlas serve every size, so they differ from a hinted rasteriser's by fractions of
			a pixel. Those fractions accumulate across a line until a word falls to the next one,
			and the wrapping paragraphs below are sized to make that happen often.

			Breaks do not survive a change of dp ratio, and are not meant to: an advance is a
			whole number of pixels at each size, so doubling the ratio halves the relative
			rounding error and words move. Compare like for like.
		*/
		body
		{
			font-family: Inter;
			font-size: 16dp;
			color: #e8e8f0;
			background-color: #16161c;
			padding: 32dp;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			box-sizing: border-box;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: row;
		}

		.column { flex: 1 1 0; padding-right: 32dp; }

		h1 { font-size: 22dp; font-weight: 600; color: #f0c674; margin-bottom: 12dp; }
		h2 { font-size: 13dp; font-weight: 600; color: #6a6a7a; margin: 16dp 0 6dp 0; }

		/* The sizes the plan sweeps, one per line, so a report entry exists for each. */
		.s10 { font-size: 10dp; }
		.s12 { font-size: 12dp; }
		.s14 { font-size: 14dp; }
		.s16 { font-size: 16dp; }
		.s20 { font-size: 20dp; }
		.s28 { font-size: 28dp; }
		.s40 { font-size: 40dp; }
		.s64 { font-size: 64dp; }
		.s96 { font-size: 96dp; }

		/* Narrow on purpose: wrapping only tells you anything when it happens often. */
		.prose { width: 340dp; color: #c8c8d4; margin-bottom: 12dp; }
		.tight { letter-spacing: 1dp; }
		.loose { line-height: 1.8; }
		.mono { font-family: RobotoMono; font-size: 14dp; color: #9ad0a0; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="column">
		<h1>Size sweep</h1>
		<div class="s10">10dp Hamburgefonstiv 0123</div>
		<div class="s12">12dp Hamburgefonstiv 0123</div>
		<div class="s14">14dp Hamburgefonstiv 0123</div>
		<div class="s16">16dp Hamburgefonstiv 0123</div>
		<div class="s20">20dp Hamburgefonstiv 0123</div>
		<div class="s28">28dp Hamburgefonstiv</div>
		<div class="s40">40dp Hamburge</div>
		<div class="s64">64dp Ham</div>
		<div class="s96">96dp Ha</div>

		<h2>Monospace</h2>
		<div class="mono">folio.Font.Report --strict 0123456789</div>
	</div>

	<div class="column">
		<h1>Wrapping</h1>

		<h2>Body</h2>
		<p class="prose">The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog while a distance field holds
		only one silhouette, and the median of three channels puts the corners back where a single
		channel would have rounded them off.</p>

		<h2>Letter spacing</h2>
		<p class="prose tight">The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog while a distance field
		holds only one silhouette, and the median of three channels puts the corners back.</p>

		<h2>Line height</h2>
		<p class="prose loose">The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog while a distance field
		holds only one silhouette, and the median of three channels puts the corners back.</p>

		<h2>Long words</h2>
		<p class="prose">Antidisestablishmentarianism pneumonoultramicroscopicsilicovolcanoconiosis
		supercalifragilisticexpialidocious</p>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
